course: dictionary
lesson: 852
title: Words about trust
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A betrayal is when someone breaks your trust. Trust means you can rely on a person to keep their word and not hurt you. Betrayal is the opposite: a friend tells your secret, lies to you, or helps your enemy.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Refusing to join a fight is not betrayal; a true friend does not ask you to get hurt or hurt others.» The clue is that a true friend does not ask you to hurt anyone, so a betrayal is what a true friend would never do.
explain: Context can also show what is not a betrayal. «Telling a grown-up about a friend in danger is help, not betrayal, even if the friend is angry at first.» The words help and keeps people safe tell you that, even when a friend is cross, it is not betrayal.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Reading someone else's messages without asking is breaking their trust.» It still makes sense, so you have understood betrayal.
fact: Betrayal is a noun. One act of betrayal is also called a betrayal.
fact: «Betrayal» means breaking someone's trust, for example by telling their secret, lying to them or helping their enemy.
fact: «Betrayal» of a country means helping its enemies. This is also called treason.
fact: To feel betrayed means you feel that someone has broken your trust.
fact: Telling a grown-up about danger is not betrayal, because it keeps people safe.
exercise: «Refusing to join a fight is not betrayal.» Which act would be a betrayal? | *Telling a friend's secret to hurt them | Saying sorry after a mistake | Telling a friend's secret to the whole class | Sharing a joke with a friend
exercise: «Telling a grown-up about a friend in danger is help, not betrayal, even if the friend is angry at first.» Is telling a grown-up a betrayal? | Yes, always | Yes, but only if it is a teacher | *No, it is help | Yes, if the friend is angry
exercise: Which meaning fits betrayal best? | Being very tired after a long day | Running very fast | *Breaking someone's trust | Giving someone a present
test: «She felt betrayed when her best friend told everyone her secret.» What does betrayed mean here? | *Felt that her trust had been broken | Very proud and happy | Cold and wet | Hungry and tired
test: «The spy gave secrets to the enemy, which is betrayal of his country.» What is betrayal of a country also called? | Friendship | Kindness | *Treason | Holidays
exam: Which one is NOT a betrayal? | Lying to a friend to get them into trouble | *Telling a grown-up that a friend is in danger | Helping your enemy against your team | Telling someone's secret to other people
